# The opening of the game: the title over the dark sea, then (on a new
# voyage) the night the lantern pulled you from it. Played by the Opening
# node in scenes/prototype/sea.tscn. Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.
#
# A cutscene is a conversation whose @ cues stage the scene. Lines wait for
# the Interact button; cues that take time (a fade, a wait, a clip) hold the
# script until they're done. Every cue is listed in
# scripts/cutscene/cue_list.gd.
#
# Where things are, so you can change them without touching this file:
# - Shots (where the camera goes) and marks (where people stand) are
#   Marker3D nodes. The bunk room's are in scenes/prototype/ship.tscn under
#   Shots and Marks; the rescue's are in scenes/prototype/intro/rescue_set.tscn.
# - Clips (@play, @start) are animations. The underwater ones are in
#   scenes/prototype/intro/underwater.tscn: open it, select Clips, and the
#   timeline at the bottom of the editor shows them. Each moves the set's
#   camera too, so a clip is also a shot.
# - Sounds (@sound) are the players under SoundCues in sea.tscn. Some have
#   no recording yet (bell, heartbeat, heartbeat_small, flare, deep_note):
#   they're silent until one is put where the player's Recording points.
# - The title is her nameboard at the stern: the letters, the hook, the
#   lantern on it and his clips (takes_watch, hears, dives, welcome) are in
#   scenes/prototype/intro/stern_watch.tscn.
# - His looks (@look) are listed in scripts/companion/lantern_face.gd.
#
# To tune one beat: set Start Section on the Opening node to its name and
# the game opens there. While it runs, F8 reads this file again and replays
# the section you're in.

# Her name. The lantern on his hook at the stern, swinging, lights the
# carved board a few letters at a time. It waits for any button. A saved
# voyage carries on from here; a new one asks who you are, then he hears
# something.
~ start
@hide heron
@play takes_watch
@look hook_lantern tired
@shot the_board cut
@fade in 3.0
@wait_for any Press any button
@sound confirm
? saved_voyage
-> carry_on
-> who_are_you

# A saved voyage: he turns from her name to the lit windows, pleased to see
# you. Then to black, and the Opening shows which day it is.
~ carry_on
@look hook_lantern pleased
@play welcome
@wait 0.8
@show heron
@fade out 0.8
@play off_watch
@shot free cut

# A new voyage: who are you, a boy or a girl? Asked over her name, and it
# waits for the answer.
~ who_are_you
@who_are_you
-> he_hears

# A quiet night first. Then he's heard something. The swinging stops. He
# leans out on his hook and looks over the water, one way and then the
# other, and finds it. He calls it to the ship, the way a lookout does.
# Nobody answers. One look back at the lit windows, and he's off the hook
# and over the side. Her name goes dark.
~ he_hears
@play takes_watch
@shot the_board cut
@look hook_lantern tired
@wait 1.6
@look hook_lantern surprised
@play hears
@wait 0.4
@look hook_lantern worried
@play looks_out
@look hook_lantern surprised
@say lantern 2.2 Someone in the water!
@wait 2.0
@look hook_lantern worried
@play glances_back
@look hook_lantern determined
@wait 0.2
@play dives
@wait 1.2
@play off_watch
-> dark

# The dark. The storm stops dead as the water closes over. You sink, limp,
# eyes shut, for longer than is comfortable. Far above, a bell: somebody
# heard him.
~ dark
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@hush on
@start sinking
@wait 2.0
@hush off
@wait 4.0
@sound bell
@wait 5.0
-> light

# The light. A small warm thing comes through the surface, a long way off,
# and drives down through the dark in three hard pushes. Each one costs
# him: he's smaller and colder with each, and reaches you nearly out. His
# weak light finds dim shapes hanging all round: lanterns, like him.
~ light
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern determined
@look sinking_lantern clear
@look sinking_lantern mended
@play lantern_appears
@play lantern_drives
@look sinking_lantern worried
@play lantern_arrives
-> reach

# The reach. A flame can't reach through glass, so he opens his own door,
# and the sea comes in. He tells you what to do. The hand forms and fails,
# and he urges you; it fails again, he looks once at the others hanging
# there, and he asks. After that he says nothing, and holds it out, for as
# long as it takes. You can take it at any moment.
~ reach
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play opens_door
@look sinking_lantern cracked
@look sinking_lantern pleading
@start pleads
@queue offered
@say lantern 2.2 Grab my hand!
@say_in 4.3 lantern 2.2 Come on. Come on.
@say_in 9.1 lantern 2.2 ...Please.
@wait_for interact Take his hand
@sound grasp
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play taken
-> out

# Out. He's spent. Black, and no sound at all, for two held seconds. Your
# heartbeat. Then, smaller, his. Your hand catches him alight again:
# everything draws in, and blooms, your eyes open, and for a moment his
# light reaches a long way down. There's no bottom to see. Hanging below
# you at every depth are more of them, fainter and fainter until the murk
# takes them. Then he turns upward and takes your weight.
~ out
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@fade out 0
@hush on
@wait 2.0
@sound heartbeat
@wait 0.9
@sound heartbeat_small
@wait 0.7
@look sinking_lantern effort
@start flares
@fade in 0
@wait 0.5
@hush off
@sound flare
@look sinking_lantern surprised
@wait 5.1
-> haul

# The haul. From above him, down the line of his arm: he drags you up in
# hard pushes, the others falling away beneath you. Lightning lands on his
# pushes and comes down past you in shafts. A very long way down there's
# an outline, and it's moving. He doesn't look. He tells you not to.
~ haul
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@start hauls
@wait 0.4
@say lantern 1.8 Hold on.
@wait 1.4
@hush on
@sound deep_note
@wait 0.4
@lightning
@wait 2.0
@say lantern 2.2 Don't look down.
@wait 1.2
@lightning
@wait 1.6
@hush off
-> rising

# The last of it: two more pushes, and the surface.
~ rising
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play rising
@fade out 0.4
-> surface

# The surface. The roles flip: he's a small ember with his door hanging open,
# the waves want him, and you hold him up out of the water, the ship
# towering over you both. He's done his part, and his eyes close.
~ surface
@stage off
@muffle off
@show castaway
@look rescued_lantern tired
@shot from_the_water cut
@fade in 0.4
@wait 2.2
@look rescued_lantern asleep
@wait 1.2
-> rail

# The rail. Lightning shows a tall thin shape up there against the sky,
# looking down at one point of warm light on a black sea: the answer to his
# shout, a minute late. It doesn't move. Then black. How you got aboard
# isn't shown: the boathook leaning by the galley door, afterwards, says it.
~ rail
@show castaway
@look rescued_lantern asleep
@place heron rail
@show heron
@shot the_rail cut
@wait 0.9
@lightning
@wait 1.8
@fade out 0.3
@hide castaway
@hide heron
@shot free cut
@play off_watch
-> title

# Black, and where we are. The captain isn't in the bunk room yet.
~ title
@hide heron
@title Somewhere at sea
@wait 2.5
@fade in 2.0
-> waking

# You wake by your bunk, the lantern across the room.
~ waking
lantern: There you are.
lantern: You were in the water. I pulled. You held on. Good holding.
lantern: I'll get you home. I know exactly where it is. Roughly.
@wait 0.6
-> doorway

# A tall shadow in the doorway: the captain, come to look you over.
~ doorway
@place heron doorway
@show heron
@face heron player
@shot doorway cut
@wait 0.8
heron: Nobody drowns on my ship. Nobody goes hungry either.
heron: You've managed the first.
-> stove

# Through to the galley: something has been left warm on the stove. While
# we look at it, the captain goes back to the fire. Then the ship is yours.
~ stove
@shot pot_on_stove
@home heron
@wait 2.5
@shot free cut
